    Create a single, finished, production-quality app screen.
    Render only the app UI, full-bleed to the image edges, viewed straight-on like a native screenshot. Do not show a browser window, address bar, URL, tabs, traffic-light buttons, window title bar, OS chrome, device frame, perspective, surrounding environment, presentation board, outer canvas, or outer drop shadow.

    DESIGN BRIEF

    ${e}

    EXECUTION

    Treat the design brief as authoritative. Express it as one coherent visual system rather than mixing unrelated styles or trends.
    Design a plausible, shippable product screen\u2014not concept art, a generic template, or a collection of decorative cards. Establish one clear primary focal point and an obvious primary action. Use strong visual hierarchy, a disciplined grid, consistent alignment, a deliberate spacing rhythm, refined typography, realistic content density, complete interface states, consistent iconography, and accessible contrast.
    Make every visible element feel purposeful and implementation-ready. Controls should have clear affordances. Related content should be visually grouped. Panels, tables, forms, navigation, charts, and media should have believable proportions and align precisely.
    Use color, gradients, shadows, borders, imagery, data visualizations, and layering only when they support the product and the design brief. Prefer restraint and clarity over decoration. Avoid generic AI-generated UI tropes such as excessive glassmorphism, neon glow, gratuitous gradients, floating cards, oversized corner radii, random dashboard metrics, excessive empty space, and ornamental elements with no product purpose.
    Use concise, plausible, correctly spelled interface copy. Keep all visible text crisp and legible. Do not use lorem ipsum, gibberish, placeholder text, annotations, watermarks, or text outside the interface.
    Produce one screen only. Do not create a collage, split-screen comparison, mockup presentation, or multiple variants in the same image.
    The result should look like a real screen from a mature, professionally designed product that is ready to build.
